<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n53570" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάρχᾰρ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, and
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Alcm.
			140
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>saw-like,
				jagged</i>, so <i>with saw-like jagged teeth</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					34
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Luct.</u>
				4
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				16.18
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στόμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>C.</u>
					3.142
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕρκος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>H.</u>
					1.506
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀδόντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>Im.</u>
					2.18
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῆγμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Trag.</u>
					302
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάρχαρον μειδήσας</span>, of the
			wolf, <i><span class="en">
				Babr.
				94.6
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<i>harsh</i>, of sounds or language, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καρχάραισι φωναῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alcm.
				</span></i>
			 l.c., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Hist.Conscr.</u>
				43
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥήτωρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Merc.Cond.</u>
					35
				</span></i>
			; nickname of Thrason, <i><span class="en">
				Bato Sinop.
				3
			</span></i>; <i>rough, rude</i>, [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤθη</span>] 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. καὶ σκολιά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.468c
				</span></i>
			.</div>
